#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-dis.md:1
msgid "llvm-dis - LLVM disassembler"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-dis.md:6
msgid "SYNOPSIS"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-dis.md:8
msgid "**llvm-dis** \\[*options*\\] \\[*filename*\\]"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-dis.md:10
msgid "DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-dis.md:12
msgid ""
"The **llvm-dis** command is the LLVM disassembler. It takes an LLVM bitcode "
"file and converts it into human-readable LLVM assembly language."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-dis.md:15
msgid ""
"If filename is omitted or specified as `-`, **llvm-dis** reads its input "
"from standard input."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-dis.md:18
msgid ""
"If the input is being read from standard input, then **llvm-dis** will send "
"its output to standard output by default. Otherwise, the output will be "
"written to a file named after the input file, with a `.ll` suffix added (any "
"existing `.bc` suffix will first be removed). You can override the choice of "
"output file using the **-o** option."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-dis.md:25
msgid "OPTIONS"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-dis.md:28
msgid ""
"Enable binary output on terminals. Normally, **llvm-dis** will refuse to "
"write raw bitcode output if the output stream is a terminal. With this "
"option, **llvm-dis** will write raw bitcode regardless of the output device."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-dis.md:34
msgid "Print a summary of command line options."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-dis.md:38
msgid ""
"Specify the output file name. If *filename* is -, then the output is sent to "
"standard output."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-dis.md:42
msgid "EXIT STATUS"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-dis.md:44
msgid ""
"If **llvm-dis** succeeds, it will exit with 0. Otherwise, if an error "
"occurs, it will exit with a non-zero value."
msgstr ""

